Abort, rather than signal an R error, when an accessor meets a freed node.

Under PROTECTCHECK the CHK() wrapper on CAR, CDR, STRING_ELT and the
other accessors detects a read of a node the collector has already
freed, and reports it with error(). Inside a fuzz harness every R error
is caught by R_ToplevelExec and the input is simply discarded, so the
one check that detects a use-after-free in R's own node heap, where
ASAN cannot see, produces no report at all. Print the message and
abort() instead; the sanitizer runtime turns that into a crash with a
stack trace at the point of use.

The other GC consistency failures already go through gc_error(), which
R_Suicide()s when _R_GC_FAIL_ON_ERROR_ is set; the harnesses set it, and
instrumentation/0004 makes R_Suicide() abort.

Instrumentation, not a fix: adapted from kevinushey/r-afl
(fatal-gc-errors.patch), reduced to the one change that matters now that
gc_error() has its own switch. Not for upstream.

diff --git a/src/main/memory.c b/src/main/memory.c
index 37ecd405e8..abeedae1da 100644
--- a/src/main/memory.c
+++ b/src/main/memory.c
@@ -157,9 +157,14 @@ attribute_hidden int R_gc_running(void) { return R_in_gc; }
 static R_INLINE SEXP CHK(SEXP x)
 {
     /* **** NULL check because of R_CurrentExpr */
-    if (x != NULL && TYPEOF(x) == FREESXP)
-	error("unprotected object (%p) encountered (was %s)",
-	      (void *)x, sexptype2char(OLDTYPE(x)));
+    if (x != NULL && TYPEOF(x) == FREESXP) {
+	/* An R error here would be caught by the fuzz harness's top-level
+	   context and look like any other rejected input.  This is memory
+	   corruption, so stop where it is found. */
+	REprintf("unprotected object (%p) encountered (was %s)\n",
+		 (void *)x, sexptype2char(OLDTYPE(x)));
+	abort();
+    }
     return x;
 }
 #else
